# Balance of payments

- In the following slides, we will construct the accounting document in which transactions between residents and non-residents are recorded.

- This document is called the Balance of Payments 

- It is compiled using double-entry accounting, whereby each transaction is recorded twice.

# Types of Transactions

The types of transactions that we will analyze to progressively build the Balance of Payments are the following:

- purchase and sale of goods and services

- purchase and sale of production factors

- Transfers of funds that do not involve purchases or sales
 
- purchase and sale of securities by

	- entities other than the national central bank

	- the National Central Bank

# Balance of Payments Sections

The Balance of Payments is divided into three sections:

- Current account

- Capital account

- Financial account

Each section includes:

- of items with a positive sign (credit items)

- of items with a negative sign (debit items)


# Accounting for transactions

- As mentioned above, each transaction generates two accounting entries

- For each of them we will highlight in the following slides:

	- the accounting item used\footnote{For reasons of space, the generic names increase/reduction of financial assets/liabilities are used in the financial account, without specifying the type of security involved.\\}

	- the section of the balance of payments involved

	- the sign of the transaction (credit or debit) 

