# The relationship between the balances of the three sections

- The use of double-entry implies the following relationship between the balances of the three sections of the Balance of Payments:

- current account balance + capital account balance = financial account balance

- However, the fact that data is collected by different institutions and that flows can occur asynchronously causes that this equality may not hold exactly in the recorded data.

- In order to balance the document, an errors and omissions item (or statistical discrepancy) is included

