GNP = value of final goods and services produced by Italian factors of production 

GDP = value of finished products and services produced in Italy


# GNP and GNI

GNI = Gross National Income

$$GNI=GNP+TUC_{in}-TUC_{out}$$

$TUC_{in} =$ current unilateral transfers from abroad

$TUC_{out} =$ current unilateral transfers abroad

\vskip1cm 
but since
$$GNP=GDP+Y_{in}-Y_{out}$$

We can write

$$GNI=GDP+Y_{in}-Y_{out}+TUC_{in}-TUC_{out}$$


# National Income

GNI is consumed or saved:

$$GNI=C_{naz}+IM+S$$

By defining $C_{tot}=C_{naz}+IM$ we can write

$$GNI=C_{tot}+S$$

# GDP and balance of payments

We express production in terms of total consumption

$$GDP=\color{blue}C_{naz}\color{black}+G+I+EX$$

$$GDP=\underbrace{C_{naz}\color{red}+IM\color{black}}_{C_{tot}}+G+I+EX\color{red}-IM\color{black}$$

$$GDP=\color{blue}C_{tot}\color{black}+G+I+EX-IM$$

# GNI and balance of payments

We therefore have

$$GNI=GDP+Y_{in}-Y_{out}+TUC_{in}-TUC_{out}$$

$$GDP=C_{tot}+G+I+EX-IM$$


substituting the second equation into the first

$$GNI=C_{tot}+G+I+\underbrace{EX-IM+Y_{in}-Y_{out}+TUC_{in}-TUC_{out}}_{\textnormal{current account balance}}$$

$$GNI=C_{tot}+G+I+CA$$

# Economic Accounts: savings

We have previously derived two expressions for GNI:

$$GNI=C_{tot}+G+I+CA$$

$$GNI=C_{tot}+S$$

From these we derive the saving identity:

$$\underbrace{C_{tot}+S}_{GNI}=\underbrace{C_{tot}+G+I+CA}_{GNI}$$

$$S=G+I+CA$$

# Economic Accounts: private savings

The previous result can be refined by considering taxes:

$$GNI-T=C_{tot}+G-T+I+CA$$

$$\underbrace{GNI-T-C_{tot}}_{S_p}=-\underbrace{(T-G)}_{S_g}+I+CA$$

A country's private saving can finance:

- Investments
- The public sector
- other countries


